    "result_text": "I've implemented the change and all 4 tests in the spec pass under `bin/e2e`.\n\n**What changed**\n- **Settling:** when a clerk settles a claim whose due is above the clerk limit, the claim now goes to PENDING instead of being refused, and the audit file gets a `CLAIM_PENDING` line. Before, a claim with no due (n/a) was also refused; now it settles directly, because scenario 2 expects that.\n- **How PENDING counts:** it counts as open everywhere: claimed and due totals, people on hold, overdue and late charges. It ignores any statement binding and shows its live figure. It keeps the \"stated\" mark, so if it is rejected it is bound to the last statement again. A statement taken while a claim is PENDING includes it.\n- **Approve:** only a steward who did not open the claim can approve it. It becomes SETTLED with its due frozen at the live figure, and the audit line is `CLAIM_APPROVED \u2026 due=<due>`.\n- **Reject:** only a steward can reject, and a reason is required. The claim goes back to OPEN and the audit line is `CLAIM_REJECTED \u2026 reason=<reason>`. The person who opened the claim can reject it, since the request only stops them approving it.\n- **Refusals:** approving or rejecting a claim that isn't PENDING, or doing so as a non-steward, shows the row's error and changes nothing. The plain Settle button does nothing to a PENDING claim.\n- **Screen:** each claim row has new Approve and Reject buttons and a reject-reason field (`claim-approve`, `claim-reject`, `claim-reject-reason`). The error messages now cover these actions.\n- **Database:** a new migration, `V27__claim_pending.sql`, rebuilds the status column so its check allows PENDING. The old check has an auto-generated name, so it couldn't simply be dropped and replaced.\n\n**One change outside the request:** scenario 2 expects bulk-open to number a person's claims newest first, the order they're listed on screen. The code numbered them oldest first, so I reversed the order in `ClaimService.bulkOpen` and updated its comment. Existing sheets will now number bulk-opened claims differently.",
